## 2. Key Decisions (and what was rejected)

These were settled in the planning conversation. Do not relitigate without checking with the user.

| Decision | Chosen | Rejected | Why |
|---|---|---|---|
| Multi-tenancy model | **Process-level** (N server processes on one box, each w/ own port + DB dir) | Logical (single process, `user_id` col scopes data) | Process-level is bulletproof isolation, ~zero code cost, no leak risk. Logical = ~6-8 weeks work, query-audit minefield, only worth it for hosted SaaS or sharing features. Neither in roadmap. |
| Auth | **Defer entirely** for scope 1 | Token / OAuth / password now | Server intended for trusted networks. Doc the assumption. Add later when hosting offering arrives. |
| Web/mobile client | **Out of scope** | Build alongside server | Electron is the only reliable browser-rendering surface (per CLAUDE.md). Web client is hypothetical, do not design for it. **Electron is everything we care about.** |
| PTY ownership | **Server owns** (local server → local PTY, remote → remote) | Client-owned, server proxy | Whole point is decoupling agent lifetime from client. |
| Worktree ownership | **Server owns** (same as PTY). Worktree root = `getDataRoot()/worktrees/<taskId>/`, override via `SLAYZONE_WORKTREE_ROOT`. | — | Consistent w/ PTY. Side effect: remote worktrees are inaccessible to local fs tools. |
| Server statefulness on restart | **PTYs die on restart** | Persistent (tmux-style detach) | Matches current Electron behavior. Big complexity add, defer. |
| Migration tool direction | **Local → remote only** | Bidirectional | Scope-1 use case is one-way move. Add reverse later if needed. |
| Migration UX | **In-app Electron wizard** | Standalone CLI command | Electron is the only client we care about. Don't build CLI-side flows for end-user features. |
| Offline mode | **Out of scope**, but use react-query in client refactor so it's possible later | Build offline-first now | Premature. react-query gives free path. |
| Agent CLI provisioning | **User installs on server box** (their API keys, their CLI binaries) | Server bundles them | Aligns w/ self-hosted scope 1. |
| User concept in DB | **Skipped** | `user_id` col scaffold | Process-level multi-tenancy makes it unnecessary. |
| **Transport** | **tRPC over WebSocket** (queries + mutations + subscriptions all over WS) | Plain HTTP+zod registry, REST, SSE | End-to-end type safety renderer↔server. Subscriptions handle streaming (PTY data, events). Single dependency. |
| **Local-mode hosting** | **Embedded in Electron main process** (server code is just imported and started in-process when local mode active) | Spawn server as child process | Simpler. No child lifecycle, no port discovery dance. Renderer still talks tRPC/WS to `localhost:<port>` — same transport as remote. One transport everywhere. |
| **Compat layer cutover** | **Rip per-phase** | Keep both transports for entire migration | Each phase replaces its IPC handlers with tRPC routes and deletes the old. No long-lived dual-transport debt. |

