## 7. Conventions to Follow

Pulled from `CLAUDE.md`, `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `PHILOSOPHY.md`, and project memory. Non-exhaustive.

- **Sustainability over simplicity**: pick the most robust long-term solution; never preserve a quick hack. But never drop existing functionality — migrate.
- **Imports from package barrels only**, not deep file paths. (memory: `feedback_slayzone_barrel_imports`)
- **No destructive git** without asking (memory: `feedback_no_destructive_git`). Manual edits to revert. No `--no-verify`. No branch switching without asking.
- **Theming**: every color via theme tokens. No raw Tailwind palette classes (`bg-neutral-*` etc.) or hex (`bg-[#1a1a1a]`). Lint enforces (`pnpm lint:theme`). Server pkg has no UI so this rarely applies, but Electron client changes do.
- **Conventional commits**: `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `release:`. Scope optional, e.g. `feat(server): bind on host`.
- **No auto-commit / no auto-publish**. Every commit and release needs explicit user approval. (memory: `feedback_no_auto_commit_v2`, `feedback_no_publish_without_approval`)
- **Plan before implement**. Get approval on a plan before writing code. (memory: `feedback_plan_before_implement`) — this asset is the plan.
- **Read skill docs before slay CLI**. Always load the relevant skill (e.g. `slay-tasks`, `slay-assets`) before invoking `slay` commands. (memory: `feedback_read_skills_first`)
- **CLI invocations need `--dev` flag** when interacting with running dev SlayZone (per CLAUDE.md). Task ID auto-injected from `$SLAYZONE_TASK_ID` if present.
- **Caveman ultra mode** for chat in this project. Apply skill at session start. Code/commits/PRs/docs (like this asset) stay normal. (CLAUDE.md)
- **TDD for bug fixes**, write failing test first. For this feature work, contract / per-handler-migration tests precede deletion of the old IPC handler.
- **E2E rules**: useRef + callback ref for DOM measurement (early returns kill `useEffect`). New tabs needed for fresh hook mounts (mounted-but-hidden tabs don't re-trigger effects). See CLAUDE.md "E2E Testing Rules" + extensive memory under `MEMORY.md` "E2E Testing".
- **Vite externalization gotcha**: new domain pkgs MUST be added to `externalizeDepsPlugin({ exclude: [...] })` in `electron.vite.config.ts` or they fail at runtime.
- **Dual-write for Provider Config** (v34+): legacy per-provider columns still written alongside `provider_config` JSON. Don't break this.
- **Diagnostics in separate DB** (`slayzone.dev.diagnostics.sqlite` via `getDiagnosticsDatabase()`). Never write `diagnostics_events` to main DB.

