## 9. Boundaries — Don't Do These

- Don't add `user_id` columns. Multi-tenancy is process-level.
- Don't add auth. Trusted-network model. Document it loud, don't implement.
- Don't build a web client. **Electron is the only client we care about.**
- Don't add TLS termination. User's reverse proxy concern.
- Don't make WCV (browser panel) work over remote. Hide UI in remote mode.
- Don't add persistent PTY (tmux-style). Out of scope.
- Don't keep IPC and tRPC in parallel as a long-lived compat layer. Rip per-phase, per-handler.
- Don't drop existing functionality to simplify a migration. Always migrate, never delete-and-rewrite.
- Don't use REST or plain HTTP for procedures. tRPC for everything.
- Don't spawn the server as a child process in local mode. Embed it in Electron main process.
- Don't build CLI flows for end-user features (like migration). In-app wizard.

